    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\calU _ c(X)$ be the partially ordered set of <em>compact</em> open subsets of $X$, let $\calP _ c(X) = \calP ( \Nerve (\calU _ c(X)) )$, and let $\Shv _ c(X)$ be the full subcategory of $\calP _ c(X)$ spanned by those presheaves $\calF $ with the following properties: 
    <p>
      <ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The object $\calF (\emptyset ) \in \calC $ is final. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every pair of compact open sets $U, V \subseteq X$, the associated diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \calF ( U \cap V) \ar [r] \ar [d] &  \calF (U) \ar [d] \\ \calF (V) \ar [r] &  \calF (U \cup V) } \]
</div>
<p>
 is a pullback. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
    <p>
      In §<a href="/tag/52073A" data-tag="52073A">7.3.5</a>, we will prove that the restriction functor $\Shv (X) \rightarrow \Shv _ c(X)$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories (Theorem <a href="/tag/B9FAF0" data-tag="B9FAF0">7.3.5.2</a>). It will therefore suffice to prove that $\Shv _ c(X)$ is compactly generated. 
    <p>
      Using Lemmas <a href="/tag/48CDAD" data-tag="48CDAD">5.5.4.19</a>, <a href="/tag/95196D" data-tag="95196D">5.5.4.17</a>, and <a href="/tag/7C6D26" data-tag="7C6D26">5.5.4.18</a>, we conclude that $\Shv _ c(X)$ is an accessible localization of $\calP _ c(X)$. Let $X$ be a compact object of $\calP _{c}(X)$. We observe that $X$ and $LX$ co-represent the same functor on $\Shv _{c}(X)$. Proposition <a href="/tag/2A38C8" data-tag="2A38C8">5.3.3.3</a> implies that the subcategory $\Shv _ c(X) \subseteq \calP _ c(X)$ is stable under filtered colimits in $\calP _ c(X)$. It follows that $LX$ is a compact object of $\Shv _0(X)$. Since $\calP _{c}(X)$ is generated under filtered colimits by its compact objects (Proposition <a href="/tag/51050B" data-tag="51050B">5.3.5.12</a>), we conclude that $\Shv _{c}(X)$ has the same property. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
